Total eggs: \(17 \times 3 \times 6 = 306\) eggs. Packing them into cartons of 12: \(306 \div 12 = 25\), with 6 eggs left over. Only the 25 full dozens can be sold: \(25 \times \$4 = \$100\).

}
}

\end{enumerate}
}

